# Pi harness

This directory is a deliberately small personal Pi harness. Only the
hand-maintained config is tracked by yadm; runtime state is ignored. The
ignore mirror is `.gitignore`, `model-fallback/` exists in it as
over-defensive (nothing in this harness uses model fallback), and the
whitelisted path list is otherwise exhaustive. Run:

    git --git-dir="$HOME/.local/share/yadm/repo.git" ls-files -- .config/pi

to see the tracked set, and `yadm status` within this tree to confirm
nothing runtime-generated is untracked there.

## Runtime (ignored) state

There are two gitignore layers, and `git check-ignore -v` reads the outer
one: this file whitelists only hand-maintained paths with `!` rules, while
the tracked `.gitignore` in this same directory (shown below) knocks out
regenerable subdirectories inside the whitelisted trees — never re-add
those subpaths by surprise (e.g. `auth.json` is already caught).

`agent/auth.json` (0600) has provider credentials. `agent/trust.json`
holds trusted-directory markers. `agent/sessions/` has per-project session
transcripts. `pi.bin` is the compiled binary itself. `.pi/` holds a
pi-regenerated runtime copy of the subagent feature flags — the tracked
`agent/subagents.json` is the hand-edited authoritative copy.
`agent/npm/` is the package checkout for extensions declared in
`settings.json`'s `packages` list plus two extras present in
`package.json` but not wired to pi: `@latentminds/pi-quotas` and
`pi-quota-monitoring`. `agent/patches/` is a local patch library:
`apply.sh` reapplies stored patches onto pi's `node_modules` after every
pi update, and the whole tree is ignored until a real patch dir justifies
tracking. The harness intentionally has no model fallback; the
`agent/model-fallback/config.json` whitelist entry is
over-defensive and stays only so a future fallback config lands tracked
by default rather than by surprise.

Configs and code under `agent/extensions/` are all tracked except the
regenerated permission-decision log, whose ignore rule is
`agent/extensions/pi-permission-system/logs/` in the rules block below
(no leading `!` — it wins as the last matching rule there). Run
`yadm status --ignored=matching -- ~/.config/pi` to see the full
ignored list.

Track a file by adding it to this whitelist (and keeping it out of the
regenerable knockouts below), not by `git add -f`.

## Modes and feature flags

`agent/subagents.json` is the hand-edited copy; pi regenerates a runtime
copy at `.pi/subagents.json` (ignored), whose lists diverge (latest:
`viewerMarkdown: all`). Treat the tracked file as authoritative. When pi
grows a new flag, the tracked copy is updated by hand.

`agent/settings.json` lists the installed packages. Two current entries
have no tracked config file: `@narumitw/pi-usage` (its footer widget
wiring lives in `agent/extensions/pi-footer.json`) and `pi-footer`
itself (tracked config at the same path).

## Extensions and the permission system

Extensions are discovered by pi in `agent/extensions/` plus the packages
in `settings.json`. Everything here is hand-maintained; the herdr bridge
files (`herdr-agent-state.ts` upstream-installed via
`herdr integration install pi`, and `herdr-ask-user-bridge.ts`) make herdr
reflect ask-user and permission dialogs, which would otherwise be
invisible in the herdr pane indicator.

The permission gate is:
- `@gotgenes/pi-permission-system` with `yoloMode: true`, `*: ask`,
  deny on secrets (`*.env*`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, `~/.ssh/*`,
  `~/.pi/agent/auth.json`), deny `sudo *`, allow-list of common safe
  commands, and per-directory external-directory rules.
- `@mzwing/pi-permission-auto-review` as its only authorizer, delegating
  to `codex-auto-review` (reasoning: low, 45 s timeout); its
  `additionalPolicy` states the operator policy for this YADM-dotfiles
  single-user Arch workstation.

Both config files and the herdr bridge are tracked; the JSONL decision
log under `pi-permission-system/logs/` is not.

`bash-readonly/` is a read-only-agent prototype: Bubblewrap mounts the
host filesystem read-only, an unprivileged OverlayFS gives each command a
disposable writable project view, and `/tmp` and cache state stay
writable. Network remains enabled (not read-only). Its nested filename
`bash-readonly.ts` deliberately avoids pi's auto-discovery patterns
(`extensions/*.ts`, `extensions/*/index.ts`) so only explorer and tester
agents load it via an explicit path; the main session never loads it.

## Omarchy-provided skills

`agent/skills/omarchy` and `agent/skills/diagnose-crash` are symlinks
into `/usr/share/omarchy/default/agents/skills/` created by Omarchy's
skills.sh and ignored by git (to git a symlink is a file, not a
directory). They do not belong in the tracked whitelist.

## Deliberately removed

`pi-automode` was replaced by the permission system in `settings.json`
packages, but its tracked config `agent/extensions/pi-automode/config.json`
stays: the classifier config (`opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash`,
`allowInsideWorkingDirectory`, reasoning `low`) is harness documentation
for an intentionally dormant component, not runtime state.

Also deliberately removed are separate leader and general modes,
`pi-plan`, default subagents, fallback agents, workflows, schedules,
nested delegation, agent mentions, fleet UI, persistent agent memory, and
output transcripts. Features return only after a repeated observed need
justifies their routing, context and maintenance cost.

## Setup and validation

- Run `/web-tools` once to configure a search provider.
- `bash-readonly` requires Linux with `bubblewrap`, unprivileged user
  namespaces, and unprivileged OverlayFS.
- `pi.bin` is current for pi 0.87.1 (`settings.json`'s
  `lastChangelogVersion` matches). Shell and environment details live in
  the dotfiles repo's `docs/environment-architecture.md`, and the
  overall harness in `~/.config/docs/harness.md`; agent-facing
  workflow lives in `agent/AGENTS.md` and `agent/skills/`.

---

# Only the hand-maintained config is version controlled. Everything else here
# is credentials, session transcripts, caches, or churn.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!agent/
!agent/AGENTS.md
!agent/README.md
!agent/settings.json
!agent/subagents.json
!agent/agents/
!agent/agents/**
!agent/skills/
!agent/skills/**
!agent/extensions/
!agent/extensions/**
!agent/model-fallback/
!agent/model-fallback/config.json

# Regenerable, even inside the whitelisted config dirs (last match wins).
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
agent/extensions/pi-permission-system/logs/
# Omarchy's skills, which omarchy/skills.sh links in. No trailing slash: to git
# a symlink is a file, not a directory.
agent/skills/omarchy
agent/skills/diagnose-crash
